1.2.7
    - added client demo recording with profile-local storage and protocol 34 output
    - added playback of classic protocol 26, 31, 32, and 34 demos, with pause and stop controls
    - added demo browsing, startup metadata, and playback launch with restored browser navigation
    - expanded base-game and mission-pack temporary effects, including cables, lightning, heatbeams, steam, and particle shells
    - improved explosion animation, particle motion, effect timing, and shared effect asset lifetimes
    - fixed content browser bookmarks across profile changes and added game-themed horizontal scrollbars

1.2.6
    - reworked networking with owned client/server transports, immutable Kotlin messages and addresses, and injected settings
    - preserved Quake II protocol 34 compatibility and reduced player updates by omitting unchanged weapon model indices

1.2.5
    - added BSP map selection to the multiplayer hosting menu and player model previews to Player Setup
    - unified standalone and browser resource previews, with external player skins, text files, and streaming cinematics
    - replaced the legacy server controller with Kotlin ServerHost and separated host, game, and per-map state ownership
    - isolated game rules, pause policy, timing, and failure handling across hosted games
    - improved save validation, entity component restoration, and recovery from failed map and load transitions
    - strengthened connection cleanup and dedicated server shutdown

1.2.4
    - added an active-profile content browser to the client menu, with image thumbnails and adjustable thumbnail sizes
    - added embedded image, sound, sprite, MD2 model, and BSP map previews with shared playback and camera controls
    - added Escape navigation through browser folders and fixed standalone WAL thumbnail palette loading
    - refined engine and game menu themes, font sizing, frames, scrollbars, and split handles
    - added UI sample capture tools and half-transparent console backgrounds
    - allowed Cake Viewer to start without arguments and fixed server handling of missing downloads

1.2.3
    - expanded Cake Viewer with PAK archive browsing, folder thumbnails, and drag-and-drop file replacement
    - added archive previews for images, sounds, sprites, MD2 models, and BSP maps
    - added TGA image support, image fit/zoom/pan, sound audition/looping, and shared animation controls
    - added MD2 skin selection, orbit and fly cameras, and richer resource information
    - kept viewer UI pixel sizing stable on resize and consolidated preview resource ownership
    - renamed cake-model-viewer to cake-viewer and fixed its native build on current GraalVM

1.2.2
    - added cake-fullgame desktop distribution with Singleplayer and Host Game menus
    - embedded server and game modules for local singleplayer and multiplayer hosting
    - kept cake-client as a remote-only client
    - added typed cvars across client, server, and game, with validated options controls
    - scaled menus and game UI through a shared virtual viewport (cvar cl_ui_size)
    - fixed air acceleration replication, instance save settings, and macOS launcher argument forwarding

1.2.1
    - added BSP lightmaps, animated textures, visibility culling, and batched world rendering
    - improved dynamic lighting, particles, weapon effects, water rendering, and positional sound
    - added persistent game-data profiles, profile editing, and automatic data-directory detection
    - added Join Game, Player Setup, and Options menus with content-themed styling
    - improved console history, completion, scrolling, and command descriptions
    - introduced a shared virtual filesystem with directory, PAK, and ZIP support, and JSON save files
    - added UDP asset downloads, screenshots, and rendering/network diagnostic graphs
    - split client and model viewer launchers into separate standard JVM distributions
    - upgraded to Java 25, Kotlin 2.4.20, and Gradle 9.8.0; updated runtime and native build tooling

1.2.0
    - introduced the Cake client built on libGDX and LWJGL3, replacing the legacy client in the active build
    - added multiplayer connectivity, keyboard/mouse bindings, and interpolated player/entity movement
    - added BSP map rendering, animated MD2 models, player and weapon models, skies, and SP2 sprites
    - added HUD layouts, inventory display, crosshairs, positional sounds, footsteps, and initial client effects
    - introduced the standalone model viewer for MD2, BSP, PCX, and WAL assets
    - migrated asset loading to libGDX AssetManager and added Apple Silicon support
    - upgraded the build baseline to Java 21

1.1.1
    - split common, game, server, client, and fullgame into separate build modules
    - enabled multiple server/game instances in one JVM by removing shared static state
    - reworked network packets and messages, with Quake 2 protocol 34 compatibility tests
    - migrated map entity logic to Kotlin and extracted item definitions into CSV data
    - added a dynamic-light flashlight to the legacy client and fixed savegame and entity behavior bugs

1.1.0
    - separated game, server, client, and common code into packages with explicit dependencies
    - added a standalone dedicated server without client libraries

1.0.0
    - gradle support
    - project cleanup
    - dropped unmaintained frameworks - jogl, joal, jsr231, applet

0.9.5

	- quake video (cinematics) support including sound streaming  
	- save games are from now on build compatible  
	- support for arbitrary sound sample rates  
	- dedicated server mode
	- lots of bugfixes

0.9.4 2005-05-26

	- multiplayer client and server functionality
	- Mac OS X support
	- webstart version
	- experimental lwjgl driver
	- standalone installer
	- online installation of Quake2 demo data files
	- mouse wheel support
	- very fast screenshot function
	- memory footprint reduced
	- bugfixes
	
0.9.3 2004-09-09

	- savegames
	- command line completion in console
	- better fullscreen vidmode selection
	- memory footprint reduced
	- improved performance
	- bugfixes
	
0.9.2 2004-06-28

	- joal sound
	- new "fastjogl" OpenGL renderer for improved performance
	- fullscreen support on windows
	- bugfixes

0.9.1 2004-05-04

